WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.600 --> 00:00:02.902
-Our next guest is
a Tony-nominated actor

00:00:02.902 --> 00:00:05.070
you know from shows like
"Spin City," "Mad About You,"

00:00:05.070 --> 00:00:07.907
and "Curb Your Enthusiasm," as
well as the movie "Inside Out."

00:00:07.907 --> 00:00:09.843
He stars in "East New York,"

00:00:09.843 --> 00:00:11.744
which airs Sunday nights
on CBS

00:00:11.744 --> 00:00:13.179
and streams on Paramount Plus.

00:00:13.179 --> 00:00:14.180
Let's take a look.

00:00:14.180 --> 00:00:15.214
-I believe in what you're doing.

00:00:15.214 --> 00:00:16.949
I understand why
you're doing it.

00:00:16.949 --> 00:00:19.418
I'm just afraid that the forces
arrayed against you

00:00:19.418 --> 00:00:21.087
may be overwhelming.

00:00:21.087 --> 00:00:23.689
-I expect to have the support
of Chief Suarez.

00:00:23.689 --> 00:00:26.559
If it's politically advangeous,
I expect to have the support

00:00:26.559 --> 00:00:28.060
of Deputy Mayor Sharpe.

00:00:28.060 --> 00:00:30.596
I also just might

00:00:30.596 --> 00:00:34.567
have the support of the people
who live in East New York.

00:00:34.567 --> 00:00:36.903
-And you have me.

00:00:36.903 --> 00:00:38.504
-Please welcome back
to the show,

00:00:38.504 --> 00:00:40.840
the one, the only Richard Kind!

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:44.010
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:44.010 --> 00:01:10.903 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:10.903 --> 00:01:13.339
-Let's get rid of this, 'cause
I want to just talk to you

00:01:13.339 --> 00:01:15.475
and not worry about
anybody who's calling.

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:16.609
I just want to talk to you.
-Okay, thank you.

00:01:16.609 --> 00:01:17.877
-'Cause we're on TV.

00:01:17.877 --> 00:01:19.145
-You do use the compass app,
though.

00:01:19.145 --> 00:01:21.914
-All the time!
And Google Maps all the time.

00:01:21.914 --> 00:01:23.549
You get out of a subway,

00:01:23.549 --> 00:01:24.617
you don't know which way
you're going.

00:01:24.617 --> 00:01:27.186
Where's Sullivan Street?
Is it north?

00:01:27.186 --> 00:01:29.188
[ Applause ]
Thank you!

00:01:29.188 --> 00:01:31.090
I'm a man of the people.

00:01:31.090 --> 00:01:32.358
-Oh, boy.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.694
Right off the bat. Right off
the bat with the pander.

00:01:34.694 --> 00:01:35.828
Congratulations!

00:01:35.828 --> 00:01:37.129
You have played so many
different roles

00:01:37.129 --> 00:01:39.165
over your career, and here you
are as a police officer.

00:01:39.165 --> 00:01:40.633
-I'm a cop.
-Wow.

00:01:40.633 --> 00:01:43.135
-I'm a New York cop.
-Look at you.

00:01:43.135 --> 00:01:45.038
-It's unbelievable,
and when I got hired --

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:48.307
my resume is, like you said,

00:01:48.307 --> 00:01:50.609
"Inside Out" and "Curb"
and comedies,

00:01:50.609 --> 00:01:52.445
and then look at what
I look like.

00:01:52.445 --> 00:01:54.848
-Yeah.
-And I walk down the street

00:01:54.848 --> 00:01:56.282
and I see some of the
New York cops

00:01:56.282 --> 00:01:59.818
with stomachs here and I go,
"Ahh, I could be a cop."

00:01:59.818 --> 00:02:02.021
-Yeah.
-Ehh, I could be a cop.

00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:04.423
And so I'm a cop. I'm a cop!

00:02:04.423 --> 00:02:06.325
-Do you like it?
-Oh, I love it.

00:02:06.325 --> 00:02:08.194
Well, first of all,
why do I like it?

00:02:08.194 --> 00:02:10.296
Because I don't have to
hold for laughs.

00:02:10.296 --> 00:02:11.997
I like that.

00:02:11.997 --> 00:02:15.601
I found out -- I was on
"Finding Your Roots,"

00:02:15.601 --> 00:02:18.170
which the show on PBS
with Henry Louis Gates.

00:02:18.170 --> 00:02:21.006
And I found out that
my great-grandfather

00:02:21.006 --> 00:02:22.975
was killed, was murdered.

00:02:22.975 --> 00:02:25.711
He and the nephew,
and you take a look at him --

00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:27.213
and this is something
I never knew --

00:02:27.213 --> 00:02:30.316
he could have been a gangster.
-Really?

00:02:30.316 --> 00:02:32.885
-What happened between
him and me?

00:02:32.885 --> 00:02:34.320
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:35.721
Why aren't I tough?

00:02:35.721 --> 00:02:37.557
Why am I not a tough guy?

00:02:37.557 --> 00:02:39.692
-Well, it didn't seem like
it worked out great for him.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:42.795
-No, but let's hope
he deserved it.

00:02:42.795 --> 00:02:44.263
-Yeah, well, you know what?

00:02:44.263 --> 00:02:45.564
That's a good way of
looking at it.

00:02:45.564 --> 00:02:48.767
-Yeah, I mean, he got murdered.

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:52.105
My grandfather was,
they called him an athlete

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:54.339
because he had his nose broken
11 times.

00:02:54.339 --> 00:02:55.708
He was a boxer.

00:02:55.708 --> 00:02:58.477
-This is your grandfather?
-My grandfather, Alvin.

00:02:58.477 --> 00:03:00.980
What happened between
him and me?

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:04.984
He was a tough guy.
11 times his nose was broken.

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:07.987
I was in a bike accident with
my friend, Bruce Stern,

00:03:07.987 --> 00:03:09.289
when I was in first grade.

00:03:09.289 --> 00:03:11.623
I fell on the sidewalk.
I broke my nose.

00:03:11.623 --> 00:03:12.992
That's all I got for it.
-Really?

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:14.360
-That's the toughest I've been.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:15.594
-And you haven't been on
a bike since.

00:03:15.594 --> 00:03:17.196
-Yeah, right. No. I have.

00:03:17.196 --> 00:03:18.597
But you know what was weird
that night?

00:03:18.597 --> 00:03:21.567
Because you stay up late,
everything broken.

00:03:21.567 --> 00:03:23.836
I watched "The Untouchables"
that night,

00:03:23.836 --> 00:03:27.240
and Al Capone,
at the end of the show --

00:03:27.240 --> 00:03:29.642
you know, the bad guy
always loses.

00:03:29.642 --> 00:03:31.210
-Yeah.
-It was a two-parter.

00:03:31.210 --> 00:03:32.879
But I don't know two-parters.

00:03:32.879 --> 00:03:35.448
I'd never seen an hour show,
much less "The Untouchables."

00:03:35.448 --> 00:03:38.918
Al Capone won.
To this day, I'm terrified.

00:03:38.918 --> 00:03:39.986
-Wow!

00:03:39.986 --> 00:03:41.253
-I was so scared
when I was a kid.

00:03:41.253 --> 00:03:42.288
-Because you were a first
grader.

00:03:42.288 --> 00:03:43.690
You'd taken a bad fall
on the bike,

00:03:43.690 --> 00:03:44.990
and then you find out
the bad guy wins.

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:46.125
-And you find out
the bad guys win.

00:03:46.125 --> 00:03:48.628
Eh, let's not talk about that.

00:03:48.628 --> 00:03:49.795
-I'm glad you managed to
work through that trauma.

00:03:49.795 --> 00:03:50.996
I want to ask,

00:03:50.996 --> 00:03:52.732
and then we're gonna take
a quick commercial break,

00:03:52.732 --> 00:03:54.600
but you've been in over
300 things.

00:03:54.600 --> 00:03:56.335
We looked at your list
of credits.

00:03:56.335 --> 00:03:59.538
I would imagine there's a wide
breadth of people who come up

00:03:59.538 --> 00:04:01.574
to you and recognize you from
different shows and films.

00:04:01.574 --> 00:04:02.908
-They do.

00:04:02.908 --> 00:04:06.378
If they're on the
East or West Coast,

00:04:06.378 --> 00:04:07.747
they come up for "Curb."

00:04:07.747 --> 00:04:10.216
If they're Jewish, it's a show
called "A Serious Man."

00:04:10.216 --> 00:04:13.152
If they're of a certain age,
it's "Mad About You."

00:04:13.152 --> 00:04:15.954
The weird thing is "Big Mouth,"
you know.

00:04:15.954 --> 00:04:17.189
[ Cheers ]
Yes.

00:04:17.189 --> 00:04:18.658
-For the kids.

00:04:18.658 --> 00:04:23.329
-But it's also the people who
don't know me but do know me,

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:24.530
and they come up --

00:04:24.530 --> 00:04:26.399
I had one last night --

00:04:26.399 --> 00:04:29.935
I had one that's great
that came up last night.

00:04:29.935 --> 00:04:31.537
A guy goes, "Oh, dude!

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:32.972
The last time I saw you

00:04:32.972 --> 00:04:35.508
was at Ringo Starr's 70th
birthday party

00:04:35.508 --> 00:04:37.110
at the Capitol Records
building."

00:04:37.110 --> 00:04:38.644
[ Laughter ]

00:04:38.644 --> 00:04:40.913
No. No.

00:04:40.913 --> 00:04:42.581
So he didn't know who I was.

00:04:42.581 --> 00:04:44.816
But the best, this is the best.

00:04:44.816 --> 00:04:47.519
"Oh, I don't --
Oh, yeah, I know!

00:04:47.519 --> 00:04:51.023
You used to run the porn stand
over on 34th Street."

00:04:51.023 --> 00:04:53.559
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:04:53.559 --> 00:04:55.395
-Now, Richard,

00:04:55.395 --> 00:04:57.663
were you around there enough

00:04:57.663 --> 00:04:59.499
that people thought you
maybe ran it?

00:04:59.499 --> 00:05:01.800
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.800 --> 00:05:04.737
-So it matters where they're
from, what age they're from.

00:05:04.737 --> 00:05:07.206
Then they know. But I can't...

00:05:07.206 --> 00:05:08.874
-You've got a lot of
other projects coming out.

00:05:08.874 --> 00:05:09.975
We're gonna talk abut them
real quick.

00:05:09.975 --> 00:05:11.210
We'll be right back
with Richard Kind.

